  "notes": "Source: FRCC current Catalog 2026-2027 (official SmartCatalogIQ), 'Forestry Technology Associate of Applied Science' My Academic Plan: Full-Time (60 cr). Hand-transcribed 2026-10-06. Full-time 4-semester sequence used (catalog also publishes a part-time 8-semester variant). Society of American Foresters (SAF) accredited. Must complete 15 credits of general education coursework including 4 credits of GT Pathways courses (preferred: ENV 1111 and BIO 2122). Minimum 4 Forestry AAS degree elective credits; no more than 6 internship/independent study credits count toward the degree. Field courses involve walking a minimum of half a mile over uneven/steep terrain. Catalog states a minimum of 60 credits to complete the degree.",
